# Reviewed secret-scan allowlist for the Skysay Gateway OSS export.
#
# Format:  <path-glob><whitespace><rule-glob><whitespace><justification>
#   - path-glob : fnmatch against the finding's path (relative to the scan root)
#   - rule-glob : fnmatch against the rule name (e.g. "public-ipv4", "*")
#   - justification : free text (required for review)
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. This file lives at the scan root of the
# STAGED tree; export_gateway.py copies it there is NOT automatic — the scanner
# also reads scripts/oss-release/.secretsallow when scanning the source tree.
#
# The scanner's built-in placeholder handling covers the expected non-secret
# text patterns:
#   * contracts/gateway-v1.yaml           `tapi_...` / `skygw_...` doc placeholders
#   * configs/asterisk/*.template         `${SIP_TRUNK_PASSWORD}` etc. env refs
#   * .env.gateway.example                empty token fields
#
# The self-host runtime also includes five CC0 WAV assets. They are binary,
# immutable, SHA-256-pinned in their exported manifest, and verified by the
# image/package tests; the scanner cannot text-scan them, so this narrow rule
# acknowledges only that reviewed binary set.
livekit_agent/audio-environment/v1/quiet-office.wav  unscanned-binary  reviewed CC0 audio asset pinned by manifest and image verification
livekit_agent/audio-environment/v1/call-centre.wav  unscanned-binary  reviewed CC0 audio asset pinned by manifest and image verification
livekit_agent/audio-environment/v1/cafe.wav  unscanned-binary  reviewed CC0 audio asset pinned by manifest and image verification
livekit_agent/audio-environment/v1/street.wav  unscanned-binary  reviewed CC0 audio asset pinned by manifest and image verification
livekit_agent/audio-environment/v1/television.wav  unscanned-binary  reviewed CC0 audio asset pinned by manifest and image verification
#
# Add an entry here ONLY after a human confirms the flagged value is genuinely
# not a secret (e.g. a vendor's published, non-secret signalling IP). Example
# (commented, not active):
#
#   contracts/gateway-v1.yaml   high-entropy-token   reviewed: example request id, not a credential
